WEBVTT

00:01.818 --> 00:04.787
Oh, come on, Chelsea.
Is this about money?

00:04.954 --> 00:07.149
I'd be happy to pay the lease
on your apartment.

00:07.323 --> 00:08.881
It's not about money, you ass.

00:09.059 --> 00:11.789
It's ridiculous that we're engaged
and not living together.

00:11.961 --> 00:14.293
Well, excuse me for being old-fashioned.

00:14.464 --> 00:16.830
I'm just not comfortable with us
living in sin.

00:17.701 --> 00:20.295
- So you think we should stop having sex?
- No, no, no.

00:20.470 --> 00:23.371
It's not the sin I object to,
it's the living in it.

00:23.907 --> 00:26.307
There is no reason to renew
the lease on my apartment...

00:26.476 --> 00:27.841
...when I'm here every night.

00:28.011 --> 00:29.706
CHARLIE:
I love having you here. I thought...

00:29.879 --> 00:31.346
You gonna eat your pickle?

00:32.582 --> 00:35.176
- I'm gonna eat my pickle.
You can crawl out whenever.

00:35.351 --> 00:38.843
You're almost done with your sandwich
and your pickle's just sitting there.

00:39.289 --> 00:41.723
- I like to eat it last.
This is not stupid, Charlie.

00:41.891 --> 00:44.359
How very European of you.

00:46.062 --> 00:48.462
Here's another pickle. Shut up.

00:48.631 --> 00:50.622
You are so full of it.

00:50.800 --> 00:53.166
Give me one reason
why I shouldn't be living here.

00:53.336 --> 00:55.736
- I can give you several.
- This ought to be good.

00:56.773 --> 00:58.570
Well, go ahead.
CHARLIE: You mean, right now?

00:58.742 --> 01:00.801
Dance, monkey, dance.

01:00.977 --> 01:03.036
Okay. Well, there's the safety issue.

01:04.514 --> 01:06.607
Keep your apartment
for the same reason...

01:06.783 --> 01:10.844
...that airplanes are equipped with oxygen
masks and cruise ships have life rafts.

01:11.020 --> 01:13.011
&lt;i>If the Titanic had enough life rafts...&lt;/i>

01:13.189 --> 01:15.851
...Leonardo and Kate would've lived
happily ever after.

01:16.659 --> 01:18.092
Oops.

01:19.562 --> 01:21.757
&lt;i>You're comparing our relationship
to Titanic?&lt;/i>

01:21.931 --> 01:23.728
Rope-a-dope, rope-a-dope.

01:23.900 --> 01:26.528
CHARLIE:
No, no, no. Of course not.

01:26.703 --> 01:31.037
P.S., that was a very romantic movie.
Thanks for making me watch it again.

01:31.207 --> 01:33.334
He's still swinging. The kid's got heart.

01:34.010 --> 01:35.875
CHARLIE: Where are you going?
Home.

01:36.045 --> 01:38.104
See? You just proved my point.

01:38.281 --> 01:42.240
Where would you go right now
if you didn't have your own apartment?

01:47.957 --> 01:50.255
Suppose you all enjoyed listening to that.

01:50.426 --> 01:51.450
- Huh?
- Beg pardon?

01:51.628 --> 01:53.095
I enjoyed it.

02:30.700 --> 02:32.065
Can't sleep, huh?

02:32.235 --> 02:33.361
No.

02:33.536 --> 02:37.165
This Chelsea-moving-in thing
is really bugging me.

02:37.340 --> 02:38.705
Why are you up?

02:38.875 --> 02:41.810
I realized you were drinking yourself
into a miserable stupor...

02:41.978 --> 02:43.843
...over this whole situation...

02:44.013 --> 02:46.277
...and I just want to be a part of that.

02:47.417 --> 02:49.044
Thanks.

02:49.219 --> 02:51.653
I hate to say it,
but I think Chelsea might be right.

02:52.188 --> 02:53.746
You don't hate to say it.

02:53.923 --> 02:58.223
Oh, did I say, "I hate to say it?"
I meant, I can't wait to say it.

03:00.563 --> 03:04.397
But I did admire how you ferociously
defended an unwinnable position...

03:04.567 --> 03:07.661
&lt;i>...by comparing your relationship
to the Titanic.&lt;/i>

03:07.837 --> 03:08.963
That was beautiful.

03:09.639 --> 03:14.008
Oh, come on, who remembers
the names of boats that don't sink?

03:14.177 --> 03:17.772
Sure, sure. I couldn't give you a zeppelin
other than the Hindenburg.

03:17.947 --> 03:19.676
Still, it was not your finest moment.

03:20.316 --> 03:22.284
There was a time it would've worked.

03:22.452 --> 03:26.149
Yeah, back when you were dating
silicone simpletons.

03:26.823 --> 03:29.383
Unfortunately,
Chelsea's too smart for your crap.

03:29.559 --> 03:33.757
Yeah, and there's not an ounce
of silicone in those babies.

03:34.230 --> 03:37.791
Shoot, I owe Berta 5 bucks.

03:39.402 --> 03:42.803
But more to the point,
why are you so afraid to have her move in?

03:43.439 --> 03:46.897
Not afraid of her moving in, that's easy.
Moving her out's the bitch.

03:47.076 --> 03:49.340
So you're already assuming
you're gonna break up?

03:49.512 --> 03:54.074
Oh, come on, what evidence is there
to suggest that it'll end any other way?

03:54.250 --> 03:57.048
Well, I think she's capable
of a long-term commitment.

03:57.220 --> 04:00.815
And you, you could change.

04:00.990 --> 04:04.084
- You don't believe that.
- No. I was just trying to be supportive.

04:04.260 --> 04:07.752
- You're not doing a very good job.
- I'm not trying very hard.

04:10.533 --> 04:11.795
Let me ask you a question.

04:11.968 --> 04:15.233
What did you think was gonna happen
when you and Chelsea got married?

04:15.405 --> 04:17.999
Honestly, I never thought that far ahead.

04:18.174 --> 04:20.369
I figured we could stretch
the engagement out...

04:20.543 --> 04:22.773
...for a couple of years and by then,
who knows?

04:22.946 --> 04:25.972
Maybe I'd die, maybe she'd get fat.

04:27.350 --> 04:31.047
Well, kudos to you for not bringing that up
in the argument.

04:31.854 --> 04:33.583
Wasn't easy.

04:36.359 --> 04:38.224
You know what you have to do,
don't you?

04:38.394 --> 04:40.794
I don't have to do anything, Alan.

04:41.264 --> 04:45.564
If not living together is a deal breaker, then
she's free to break off the engagement...

04:45.735 --> 04:47.100
...and go on her merry way.

04:47.270 --> 04:49.329
She most certainly is.

04:50.406 --> 04:51.964
So you know what you have to do.

04:52.141 --> 04:54.666
Yes, I know what I have to do.

04:55.645 --> 04:58.808
- Are you done torturing me?
- Almost.

05:02.051 --> 05:05.111
I'm the king of the world!

05:08.658 --> 05:10.421
Okay, now I'm done.

05:26.376 --> 05:28.276
Here.

05:29.245 --> 05:30.269
What's this?

05:30.780 --> 05:32.941
Alan's house key.

05:36.819 --> 05:38.309
Why?

05:38.488 --> 05:41.946
Because I want you to move in,
and I didn't have time to make a new one.

05:43.326 --> 05:46.056
Plus, he kind of pissed me off last night.

05:47.296 --> 05:48.456
You want me to move in?

05:48.631 --> 05:51.828
Yes.
I thought about it and you were right.

05:52.535 --> 05:53.763
Uh-huh.

05:53.936 --> 05:57.167
Which is not to say I was wrong, but, uh...

05:59.208 --> 06:01.199
Okay, I was wrong.

06:02.211 --> 06:03.940
You're sure you want me to move in?

06:04.514 --> 06:06.505
Absolutely not.

06:09.852 --> 06:14.551
But I figure, what the hell? I mean,
it's gonna happen sooner or later, right?

06:15.324 --> 06:18.487
Oh, shut up.
Come on in, I'll make some coffee.

06:26.836 --> 06:28.030
What's all this?

06:29.005 --> 06:30.973
Let's just say I had faith in you.

06:31.407 --> 06:32.738
Oh.

06:34.410 --> 06:36.401
Oh...

06:38.948 --> 06:41.348
Eww.

06:44.854 --> 06:48.483
Those go upstairs in the master bedroom.
Careful, they're fragile.

06:50.960 --> 06:53.724
Okay, you and me need to talk.

06:54.363 --> 06:55.955
I know, I know.

06:56.132 --> 06:57.463
You didn't sign up for this.

06:57.633 --> 06:58.827
You work for me, not her.

06:59.001 --> 07:02.198
And it's bad enough you have to put up
with Zippy and the chimp.

07:03.739 --> 07:07.505
No. I like her better than you.
So from now on, I'm working for her.

07:09.011 --> 07:11.241
- What?
- You need something, you ask her.

07:11.414 --> 07:13.507
She talks to me, we decide.

07:14.050 --> 07:16.416
- I don't get a vote?
- Yeah, you get a vote.

07:16.586 --> 07:17.678
One vote out of three.

07:18.754 --> 07:20.517
Good luck with that.

07:37.673 --> 07:39.641
Oh, boy.

07:39.809 --> 07:41.367
You like it?

07:41.878 --> 07:43.709
Oh, boy.

07:44.814 --> 07:46.714
Don't the colors just liven the place up?

07:48.184 --> 07:49.742
Well...

07:50.353 --> 07:51.684
Uh...

07:52.455 --> 07:54.286
Oh, boy.

07:54.757 --> 07:57.282
Come on, I wanna show you
what I did in the bathroom.

07:57.460 --> 07:59.291
Oh, boy.

08:06.435 --> 08:08.096
What do you think?

08:08.871 --> 08:10.566
I don't know.

08:11.040 --> 08:14.976
I have this sudden urge
to pee sitting down.

08:16.012 --> 08:18.037
You like the new towels?

08:18.814 --> 08:20.372
I guess.

08:20.550 --> 08:24.418
- What was wrong with the old ones?
- They didn't match my shower curtain.

08:25.588 --> 08:28.955
- What was wrong with my shower curtain?
- It didn't match your towels.

08:29.125 --> 08:30.820
Maybe that's how I tell them apart.

08:34.397 --> 08:39.835
Oh. Oh, please, tell me that's one
of those Zen sand gardens.

08:42.104 --> 08:45.005
You know very well
that's Sir Lancelot's litter box.

08:45.174 --> 08:47.506
- You brought the cat?
- Of course I brought the cat.

08:47.677 --> 08:50.612
- What did you think I was gonna do?
- I don't know.

08:50.780 --> 08:52.839
Return him to the wild?

08:54.250 --> 08:55.376
You're being ridiculous.

08:55.551 --> 08:59.612
Is it ridiculous to want the turds
in my bathroom to be human?

09:01.157 --> 09:03.489
Fine, we'll put it in the laundry room.

09:03.926 --> 09:05.860
Near my clean clothes? Forget it.

09:06.028 --> 09:07.655
So where am I supposed to put it?

09:07.830 --> 09:11.231
Oh, I don't think you really want me
to tell you where to put it.

09:13.135 --> 09:15.296
CHARLIE:
I'm just saying it's too much.

09:15.471 --> 09:18.463
Pillows, towels, shower curtains,
cat crap.

09:18.641 --> 09:21.166
I don't like it. I don't need it.
I don't want it.

09:21.344 --> 09:23.574
What do you want me to do?
You want me to leave?

09:23.746 --> 09:26.340
CHARLIE:
No, no. No. You just got here. I'll leave.

09:26.515 --> 09:29.643
It'll make more room for you
and Sir Crapsalot.

09:29.819 --> 09:31.548
Charlie.

09:33.689 --> 09:35.589
- Get a good earful?
- No.

09:35.758 --> 09:39.353
I did. And I don't appreciate
being called Sir Crapsalot.

09:43.733 --> 09:45.997
Good. For some reason,
I can't find my house key.

09:47.536 --> 09:50.334
I hope you're happy with yourself.

09:50.873 --> 09:53.137
Why would I start now?

10:06.555 --> 10:07.920
Hey.

10:09.759 --> 10:11.920
- How'd you find me?
- Wasn't hard.

10:12.595 --> 10:16.622
When you're not volunteering to read stories
or feed the homeless, you're usually here.

10:17.767 --> 10:20.429
Bay Breeze, extra pineapple.

10:23.706 --> 10:26.300
I'm not cut out
for this living-together stuff, Alan.

10:26.475 --> 10:29.103
- I mean, I tried, I really tried.
- That's true.

10:29.278 --> 10:33.146
You gave it a whole hour
and 20 minutes.

10:34.250 --> 10:36.946
Hey, now Berta owes me 5 bucks.

10:37.653 --> 10:40.952
Charlie, it's not really that difficult
to live with a woman.

10:41.390 --> 10:43.950
Says the man
who's been thrown out twice.

10:44.126 --> 10:46.458
I didn't say it wasn't hard for them.

10:48.297 --> 10:51.494
Did you see the salt-and-pepper shakers
Chelsea put in the kitchen?

10:51.667 --> 10:52.691
No.

10:52.868 --> 10:55.268
They're like these foot-high
ceramic roosters...

10:55.438 --> 10:57.838
...with little S and P holes in their beaks.

10:58.007 --> 11:00.976
Oh, cute. I think I saw those
in the Williams-Sonoma catalog.

11:01.977 --> 11:05.469
What am I freaking out about? A woman's
been living with me for six years.

11:07.850 --> 11:09.613
Cheap shot. Oh.

11:09.785 --> 11:10.843
Canned pineapple?

11:14.690 --> 11:16.954
It's not just the salt shakers.

11:17.126 --> 11:20.789
It's the fancy pillows on the bed,
the fruity towels in the bathroom.

11:20.963 --> 11:24.364
And then there's the clothes
and the shoes. Oh, my God, the shoes.

11:24.533 --> 11:26.592
She's got almost as many as I do.

11:28.237 --> 11:32.833
And lest we forget, she brought her big,
fat, pooping cat to live with us.

11:33.442 --> 11:36.240
As opposed to what,
having it put to sleep?

11:36.412 --> 11:39.506
I suggested letting it go.
I didn't even think of that.

11:40.716 --> 11:44.516
The cat aside, you do know it was wrong
to storm out the way you did.

11:44.687 --> 11:47.315
Of course I know.
I'm an ass, not an idiot.

11:47.757 --> 11:49.657
One does not preclude the other.

11:51.527 --> 11:54.462
You realize this has nothing to do
with the cat or the towels...

11:54.630 --> 11:55.961
...or the pillows, don't you?

11:57.767 --> 11:59.291
Tell you what.

12:00.035 --> 12:01.161
Here's 20 bucks.

12:01.337 --> 12:03.134
Don't tell me what it's really about.

12:04.740 --> 12:08.301
Boy, you're putting me
in a tough spot here, Charlie.

12:09.145 --> 12:10.976
- Forty.
- Goodnight.

12:12.782 --> 12:16.343
Nah. I care too much about you two kids.
Here.

12:16.519 --> 12:18.646
Now, the reason you panicked
is that you real-

12:18.821 --> 12:19.913
This is just 20.

12:20.423 --> 12:23.051
Is it? Oh.

12:23.225 --> 12:24.954
My mistake.

12:29.131 --> 12:31.998
The reason you panicked and ran away...

12:32.168 --> 12:35.433
...is that you recognize
that the old Charlie is dying.

12:35.604 --> 12:40.064
But what you have to understand is he has
to die in order for a new Charlie to be born.

12:41.010 --> 12:42.807
That makes sense.

12:42.978 --> 12:45.003
- Let me ask you a question.
- Of course.

12:45.181 --> 12:47.615
Does the new Charlie
still have the old brother?

12:49.018 --> 12:51.111
Absolutely. And he's here for you.

12:51.287 --> 12:52.754
Man, I can't catch a break.

12:56.225 --> 12:59.251
So how pissed off was Chelsea
when I left?

12:59.428 --> 13:01.328
It was pretty bad at first.

13:01.497 --> 13:04.159
Did you really suggest that she do
something impossible...

13:04.333 --> 13:05.823
...with the kitty-litter box?

13:06.001 --> 13:08.595
I didn't suggest anything.
She may have inferred.

13:10.606 --> 13:13.734
I think I may have been able
to smooth it over for you a little bit.

13:13.909 --> 13:15.069
Really? What did you say?

13:15.511 --> 13:19.572
I said you had the maturity of a 9-year-old
and that she had to make allowances.

13:19.748 --> 13:22.808
That's good.
That's good, make it her fault.

13:23.519 --> 13:28.513
So now all you have to do is go home,
admit that you're a frightened little man...

13:28.691 --> 13:31.819
...who doesn't deserve her love,
and beg for her forgiveness.

13:32.461 --> 13:34.326
Groveling comes easy for you,
doesn't it?

13:34.497 --> 13:38.024
Not at first. I didn't really hit my stride
till my second marriage.

13:39.502 --> 13:41.936
Oh, by the way,
have you seen my house key anywhere?

13:42.104 --> 13:43.298
CHARLIE:
Nope.

13:47.209 --> 13:48.676
Oh, Chelsea...

13:48.844 --> 13:51.005
...I was such a fool.

13:52.915 --> 13:55.975
Thank God my brother talked some sense
into me.

13:56.986 --> 13:59.477
Oh, Charlie, I love your brother.

13:59.855 --> 14:02.050
He's so smart and masculine...

14:02.224 --> 14:06.752
...and yet his feminine side
makes him sensitive and intuitive.

14:07.363 --> 14:10.127
You're right.
I only tease him because I'm jealous.

14:10.866 --> 14:12.925
And secretly gay.

14:19.074 --> 14:20.098
Oh, hello.

14:20.843 --> 14:21.935
Don't worry.

14:22.111 --> 14:26.241
This ain't the most embarrassing thing
I ever walked in on you doing.

14:27.616 --> 14:30.210
Oh, yeah. Thanks for not making
a big thing about that.

14:30.386 --> 14:32.251
Right back at you.

14:36.191 --> 14:39.592
You know, I really should cut down
on the talking to myself.

14:39.862 --> 14:42.695
Yes, you should.
It's getting a little weird.

14:49.838 --> 14:53.137
Son of a bitch.

14:53.642 --> 14:55.906
Can I say I'm sorry again,
or are you sick of it?

14:56.378 --> 14:58.312
Mm. Say it again. Let's see.

14:58.814 --> 15:00.008
I'm sorry.

15:00.616 --> 15:02.481
Nope. Still fun.

15:04.320 --> 15:05.719
And?

15:06.188 --> 15:08.554
And I'm a big, stupid jerk.

15:09.124 --> 15:10.182
And?

15:10.359 --> 15:16.025
And I'd really like to go upstairs
and finish this apology with my mouth.

15:20.369 --> 15:21.996
Charlie, a moment.

15:23.839 --> 15:24.897
Not now, Alan.

15:25.441 --> 15:29.400
Yeah, well, there's a bit of a situation,
and I'm afraid I'm gonna have to insist.

15:29.878 --> 15:31.004
I better talk to him.

15:31.180 --> 15:32.841
He's about to go full fruit fly.

15:37.386 --> 15:40.514
- What is your problem?
- I noticed you put a lot of stuff in my room.

15:40.689 --> 15:42.953
I was wondering
how long it was gonna stay there.

15:43.125 --> 15:45.559
I've been wondering the same thing
about you.

15:45.728 --> 15:47.787
How am I supposed to live in that room...

15:47.963 --> 15:50.454
...if you and Chelsea
are gonna use it as a closet?

15:50.633 --> 15:53.033
Tell you what,
I'll give you a break on the rent.

15:53.202 --> 15:56.365
- I haven't been paying rent.
- There it is.

15:57.706 --> 15:59.298
Fine, I'll manage somehow.

16:00.009 --> 16:01.408
- Alan, wait.
- What?

16:01.944 --> 16:04.037
I need you to pull your car
out of the garage.

16:04.213 --> 16:05.737
- Why?
- You don't expect Chelsea...

16:05.914 --> 16:09.372
- ...to park on the street, do you?
- So I have to park on the street?

16:09.551 --> 16:12.042
You don't have to.
You can park it at your place.

16:12.221 --> 16:15.122
- I don't have a place.
- There it is.

16:18.360 --> 16:20.385
Leave your clicker on the coffee table.

16:20.562 --> 16:23.554
Wait, wait, Charlie.
If I don't have a clicker and a house key...

16:23.732 --> 16:27.293
- ...how am I supposed to get in?
- There it is.

16:35.144 --> 16:37.271
I don't have to pee.

16:42.484 --> 16:44.975
I don't have to pee.

16:46.522 --> 16:48.422
Damn it, I have to pee.

17:06.608 --> 17:08.200
Ow.

17:08.377 --> 17:10.470
Son of a bitch.

17:10.646 --> 17:12.739
Ski poles. Ski poles.

17:21.724 --> 17:23.248
Ow.

17:44.379 --> 17:47.940
Oh, good, a litter box.

17:52.087 --> 17:54.521
This is delicious.

17:54.690 --> 17:55.816
Sure is.

17:56.258 --> 17:58.886
Glad you like it. There's plenty more.

18:02.264 --> 18:05.631
Jake, would you pass me the chicken?

18:06.435 --> 18:07.663
It's fish, Dad.

18:08.871 --> 18:10.771
Hope you're not allergic to Sir Lancelot.

18:10.939 --> 18:14.375
I'll be fine as long as he doesn't sleep
on my face again.

18:15.744 --> 18:17.405
He is a snuggler, isn't he?

18:17.946 --> 18:21.712
Yeah. By the way, do you know
if anybody rented your old apartment yet?

18:21.884 --> 18:23.875
Actually somebody just scooped it up.

18:24.186 --> 18:26.381
- Oh.
- Why, are you thinking of moving out?

18:26.555 --> 18:28.955
There's not a lot of room for me here.

18:29.124 --> 18:31.558
- What's a place like that go for?
- Eighteen hundred.

18:31.727 --> 18:34.787
On the other hand,
it's nice to be close to family.

18:35.364 --> 18:37.298
Boy, you've got no shame at all,
do you?

18:39.134 --> 18:41.762
I assume that's a rhetorical question.

18:42.371 --> 18:43.429
Where's Uncle Charlie?

18:43.605 --> 18:47.041
- Said he had some sort of meeting.
- That means poker or strip club.

18:51.647 --> 18:53.114
I'm sure it's poker.

18:58.086 --> 18:59.417
&lt;i>- used to that type of thing.&lt;/i>

18:59.588 --> 19:02.386
&lt;i>So if they show up with some
sloppy ball-handling, we'll see.&lt;/i>

19:07.029 --> 19:08.963
Pizza.

19:15.637 --> 19:17.798
Hey, Gordon. Small world.

19:17.973 --> 19:21.966
- Hey, Mr. Harper, what are you doing here?
- Oh, I just rented this place.

19:22.144 --> 19:24.237
Decided I needed a weekend getaway.

19:24.613 --> 19:26.513
From Malibu?

19:28.417 --> 19:31.318
You'd be surprised.
It gets crowded sometimes.

19:31.854 --> 19:32.980
Okay.

19:33.155 --> 19:35.589
What happened to the woman
that used to lived here?

19:35.757 --> 19:37.657
She lives with me in Malibu.

19:37.826 --> 19:38.986
We're engaged.

19:39.394 --> 19:42.295
- And you're hanging out here all alone?
- Yep.

19:44.566 --> 19:46.466
- You know what you are, Mr. Harper?
- What?

19:46.902 --> 19:48.335
A genius.

19:50.105 --> 19:51.697
Thanks, Gordon. Good night.

19:51.874 --> 19:53.136
Good night.

19:56.011 --> 19:59.037
It's nice when someone gets you.
